  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f2bed5e614b0dd34485c43fa9f9413fc, type: 3}
  m_Name: 01_ElectrolyteDispensingAndCallAssembly
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  subject: Electrolyte Dispensing and Cell Assembly
  sender: Message
  content: "Dear Student,\n\r\nI nearly forgot to mention something important: once
    you've placed all the parts on the tray and evacuated the\r\nvacuum chamber,
    you'll find that the electrolyte dispenser is already inside. It\u2019s a fairly
    precise tool\u2014just click it\r\nonce, and it should release a single drop
    of electrolyte onto the cathode (aim is important here).\n\r\nIt\u2019s essential
    that you assemble the PAT-Cell\xAE correctly, or the cell won\u2019t function
    as intended. Fortunately, all\r\nparts are designed to interlock, so improper
    assembly is nearly impossible. Still, if the schematic leaves you\r\nuncertain,
    here\u2019s a step-by-step list to guide you:\n\r\nBase \u2192 Lower Plunger
    \u2192 Lower Cathode \u2192 Plastic Sleeve \u2192 Drop of Electrolyte \u2192
    Upper Cathode \u2192 Upper\r\nPlunger \u2192 Washer \u2192 Gear \u2192 Brass
    Top\n\r\nOnce the assembly is complete, carefully remove the cell from the vacuum
    chamber (and I do mean carefully\u2014\r\nplease don\u2019t repeat last semester\u2019s
    incident) and place it into the docking station inside the test oven.\n\r\nYour
    favorite docent,\n\r\nH. Graunt"
  maxMailSize: 185
  questOrder: 1
